„­bible_version£KJV¤book*§chapter¨sections™…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}Then Jesus six days before the passover came to Bethany, where Lazarus was which had been dead, whom he raised from the dead.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlThere they made him a supper; and Martha served: but Lazarus was one of them that sat at the table with him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸Then took Mary a pound of ointment of spikenard, very costly, and anointed the feet of Jesus, and wiped his feet with her hair: and the house was filled with the odour of the ointment.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVThen saith one of his disciples, Judas Iscariot, Simon's son, which should betray him,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNWhy was not this ointment sold for three hundred pence, and given to the poor?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThis he said, not that he cared for the poor; but because he was a thief, and had the bag, and bare what was put therein.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQThen said Jesus, Let her alone: against the day of my burying hath she kept this.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@For the poor always ye have with you; but me ye have not always.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verse	ªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©Much people of the Jews therefore knew that he was there: and they came not for Jesus' sake only, but that they might see Lazarus also, whom he had raised from the dead.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
