„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPbecause that by reason of him many of the Jews went away, and believed on Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlOn the next day much people that were come to the feast, when they heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtook branches of palm trees, and went forth to meet him, and cried, Hosanna: Blessed is the King of Israel that cometh in the name of the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd Jesus, when he had found a young ass, sat thereon; as it is written,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNFear not, daughter of Sion: behold, thy King cometh, sitting on an ass's colt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿These things understood not his disciples at the first: but when Jesus was glorified, then remembered they that these things were written of him, and that they had done these things unto him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzThe people therefore that was with him when he called Lazarus out of his grave, and raised him from the dead, bare record.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZFor this cause the people also met him, for that they heard that he had done this miracle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwThe Pharisees therefore said among themselves, Perceive ye how ye prevail nothing? behold, the world is gone after him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNAnd there were certain Greeks among them that came up to worship at the feast:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwthe same came therefore to Philip, which was of Bethsaida of Galilee, and desired him, saying, Sir, we would see Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIPhilip cometh and telleth Andrew: and again Andrew and Philip tell Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[And Jesus answered them, saying, The hour is come, that the Son of man should be glorified.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Verily, verily, I say unto you, Except a corn of wheat fall into the ground and die, it abideth alone: but if it die, it bringeth forth much fruit.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqHe that loveth his life shall lose it; and he that hateth his life in this world shall keep it unto life eternal.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡If any man serve me, let him follow me; and where I am, there shall also my servant be: if any man serve me, him will my Father honour.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxNow is my soul troubled; and what shall I say? Father, save me from this hour: but for this cause came I unto this hour.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{Father, glorify thy name. Then came there a voice from heaven, saying, I have both glorified it, and will glorify it again.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnThe people therefore, that stood by, and heard it, said that it thundered: others said, An angel spake to him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOJesus answered and said, This voice came not because of me, but for your sakes.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRNow is the judgment of this world: now shall the prince of this world be cast out.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAnd I, if I be lifted up from the earth, will draw all men unto me.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ2This he said, signifying what death he should die.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book*§chapter«first_verse"ªlast_verse$¦verses“„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢The people answered him, We have heard out of the law that Christ abideth for ever: and how sayest thou, The Son of man must be lifted up? who is this Son of man?¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ½Then Jesus said unto them, Yet a little while is the light with you. Walk while ye have the light, lest darkness come upon you: for he that walketh in darkness knoweth not whither he goeth.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜While ye have light, believe in the light, that ye may be the children of light. These things spake Jesus, and departed, and did hide himself from them.¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book*§chapter«first_verse%ªlast_verse+¦verses—„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRBut though he had done so many miracles before them, yet they believed not on him:¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙIThat the saying of Esaias the prophet might be fulfilled, which he spake,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#Lord, who hath believed our report?¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ3And to whom hath the arm of the Lord been revealed?¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙATherefore they could not believe, because that Esaias said again,¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ5He hath blinded their eyes, and hardened their heart;¦layout ‚¤textÙJThat they should not see with their eyes, nor understand with their heart,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text±And be converted,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text·And I should heal them.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBThese things said Esaias, when he saw his glory, and spake of him.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£Nevertheless among the chief rulers also many believed on him; but because of the Pharisees they did not confess him, lest they should be put out of the synagogue:¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=for they loved the praise of men more than the praise of God.¦layout ªlast_verse+…¤book*§chapter«first_verse,ªlast_verse2¦verses—„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\Jesus cried and said, He that believeth on me, believeth not on me, but on him that sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,And he that seeth me seeth him that sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^I am come a light into the world, that whosoever believeth on me should not abide in darkness.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd if any man hear my words, and believe not, I judge him not: for I came not to judge the world, but to save the world.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“He that rejecteth me, and receiveth not my words, hath one that judgeth him: the word that I have spoken, the same shall judge him in the last day.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„For I have not spoken of myself; but the Father which sent me, he gave me a commandment, what I should say, and what I should speak.¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd I know that his commandment is life everlasting: whatsoever I speak therefore, even as the Father said unto me, so I speak.¦layout ªlast_verse2